note(40,"""**Content and marks.** Manuscript XIII, archive 39. Proof of XV, then induction on card S(Γ)−2, with the triangle case and definitions of U and V. No date, title sheet or total count. A long unlabelled pen stroke lies at the lower right and is retained in TikZ.

**040-N1 — proof of XV.** The intended connected-component argument is sound once the interiors meet: int Λ² avoids Λ¹, so it lies in one complementary component; a point in both interiors selects int Λ¹. Along the common open edge, equality of the exterior half-disks gives equality of the interior half-disks. The displayed chain actually repeats `D_x∩ext Λ¹` twice; the second should involve Λ² for that inference. Both exponents visibly read 1 and are preserved. The reference `def.1` is also preserved, although surrounding pages cite definition 2 for condition b).

**040-N2 — global boundary slip.** The written b) `Λ²−{s,s′}=Γ²_{s,s′}−{s,s′}` cannot hold: Λ² also contains the common open edge ]s,s′[, which is not in the open Γ² arc. Likewise the scan 39 global containment with Λ²−{s,s′} includes points of the boundary Λ¹ in its interior. The manuscript’s interlinear Γ² correction on 39 suggests the intended open-arc version. These are authorial slips, not changes to the transcript.

**040-N3 — definition of U, checked on crop.** The final exponent in `Γ²_ss′∩int Λ²` is unequivocally 2. Since Γ²_ss′ lies on Λ², this intersection is empty for a J-polygon. Thus, literally, U=int Λ¹−int Λ² contains the nonendpoint Γ² arc, which lies in Γ; it cannot serve as a subset of the complement of Γ. The formula is retained exactly. **040-N3-refined:** replacing the last `int Λ²` by `int Λ¹` removes that arc and resolves this particular boundary inclusion defect; this is an editorial observation only, not a claimed complete repair of the proof.

**040-N4 — boundedness.** The final boundedness statements do follow from the stated inclusions and inductive hypotheses: V contains the unbounded ext Λ¹, and U is contained in the relatively compact int Λ¹. This does not cure the defect in the definition of U.

**Authorial language and revisions.** Inserted “on”, triangle-case sentence, `i=1,2`, and “avec le lemme XV”; four ext/int overwrites. The unusual `Γ = au bord`, “absurd”, “generalité”, and accent variants remain. No explicit “à vérifier” or question mark occurs here.""")
